From: Android VirtIO maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] virt-common: start SurfaceFlinger after EGL selection

The graphics detector runs during early-boot. Its property actions can be
queued after boot's class_start core, starting SurfaceFlinger without an EGL
implementation and causing a fatal error followed by a five-second restart.

Use init's disabled-service handling to defer this service until the selected
EGL implementation is published. enable also handles selection before core's
class start. This follows the allocator's existing device-init gating model.

diff --git a/configs/init/init.virt.rc b/configs/init/init.virt.rc
--- a/configs/init/init.virt.rc
+++ b/configs/init/init.virt.rc
@@ -30,6 +30,13 @@
 # Graphics
+# The detector's property actions may run after class_start core.
+on init
+    stop surfaceflinger
+
+on property:ro.hardware.egl=*
+    enable surfaceflinger
+
 on property:ro.vendor.graphics=mesa
     setprop ro.hardware.egl mesa
 
 on property:ro.vendor.graphics=mesa_swrast
     setprop ro.hardware.egl mesa
